  <issue>
  [Feature Request] Print output on how to validate challenges with --debug-challenges
Can you please add a parameter, that keeps certbot running after the challenge is served in standalone mode?
So that the internal webserver is still running, that would simplify debugging complex network issues.
Currently with "--debug-challenge --test-cert", one is asked to press return *before* the internal webserver is up. And after one pressed return it exites immediately after the challenge is completed or has failed.
Or just add a "--debug-internal-webserver" parameter that starts the internal webserver, serves a debug page, shows it's url and waits until it gets killed.
  </issue>
  
